That's a great start! A navbar with a logo on the left and three links is a common layout. Since you're comfortable with CSS, we can build on that.

Let's start with the basic structure. Here's a simple example:

```html
<nav>
  <div class="logo">Logo</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Home</li>
    <li>About</li>
    <li>Contact</li>
  </ul>
</nav>
```

To make the logo stick to the top and the links stack vertically, you can use Flexbox:

```css
.navbar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
}

.logo {
  flex: 1;
}

ul {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}

li {
  margin: 0 10px;
}
```

This will place the logo on the left, the links stacked vertically, and the space between them controlled by `justify-content: space-between`.

If you want the links to be horizontal instead, you can adjust the `justify-content` property.

