I can help you create a three-column grid with a sticky sidebar. Here's a complete example:

```html
<div class="container">
  <div class="sidebar">Sidebar content goes here...</div>
  <div class="main">
    <div class="column">Column 1</div>
    <div class="column">Column 2</div>
    <div class="column">Column 3</div>
  </div>
</div>
```

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;
  height: 100vh;
}

.sidebar {
  flex: 1;
  height: 100%;
  border-right: 1px solid #ccc;
}

.main {
  flex: 2;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  height: 100%;
}

.column {
  flex: 1;
}
```

This creates a three-column layout where the sidebar takes up one-third of the height, and the main content takes up the remaining two-thirds. The sidebar is sticky by default, so it stays in place as you scroll down the main content.

If you want the sidebar to be fixed at the top instead of sticking to the main content, you can use `position: sticky; top: 0;` on the sidebar.

