`margin` is the space outside an element, while `padding` is the space inside an element.

- `margin` controls spacing around an element (top, bottom, left, right)
- `padding` controls spacing inside an element (top, bottom, left, right)

```css
.container {
  margin: 20px;
  padding: 10px;
}
```

This means the container has 20px around it and 10px inside.

